{
  "_comment": "R-Cade touch keypad (GRS Build-A-Cade FU / Viper SBC): cyd_daemon.py --profile rcade, or config.json \"profile\": \"rcade\"; long-press the display to open it. Page R-CADE presses controller buttons on the virtual gamepad 'cyd-pad' (\"pad:...\" keys, needs \"virtual_gamepad\": true, which the rcade profile sets). Map cyd-pad once in R-Cade's controller/input settings (page PAD SETUP has every button) and give it SELECT as its hotkey. The combos are R-Cade's documented ones (https://www.retro-center.com/about-r-cade/ FAQ): exit game = hotkey (usually select) + start; save state = hotkey + West (usually Y); load state = hotkey + North (usually X); RetroArch menu = hotkey + South (usually B); arcade coin = select. R-Cade names buttons Nintendo-style (South = B, East = A, West = Y, North = X); the labels show both. KEYBOARD and MAME pages send keys on the virtual keyboard 'cyd-keypad': R-Cade has its own keyboard mapping (Input menu) that is not published, so those keys are the MAME / RetroArch defaults and are TO-VERIFY on R-Cade. Warning from the R-Cade FAQ: pressing Esc 6 times switches R-Cade between its keyboard and remote-control mappings. watch_processes is empty: open the keypad by long-press (2 s).",
